<description>
Compact the checkerboard's moving color toward the edge marked by the teal pixel, leaving a maroon swept trail on the marker line.

Input structure
- A blue/black checkerboard with exactly one teal marker replacing a blue pixel on a non-corner edge.
- The marker's checkerboard parity identifies the moving color (blue); the opposite parity is background (black).

Rule
- If the marker is on the left or right edge, compact moving-color pixels in every row toward that side.
- If the marker is on the top or bottom edge, compact moving-color pixels in every column toward that side.
- Preserve the teal marker at its edge cell.
- On the marker's row or column, color cells swept by shifted moving pixels maroon unless the final compacted line occupies them.

Key insight
The marker selects both the compression direction and the checkerboard color class that moves; maroon records the movement trail only along that marked line.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "moving-color pixels of the two-color checkerboard; the teal edge marker identifies the moving-color parity",
  "path": "straight along each row toward a left/right marker edge, or along each column toward a top/bottom marker edge",
  "trajectory": "stably compact all moving-color pixels to the marker edge in every parallel line",
  "transform": "preserve the teal marker at its edge cell; on the marker row or column recolor swept vacated cells maroon unless occupied by the final compacted line"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 3-8 rows x 3-8 cols, output same size as input
  checkerboard:
    two colors in strict checkerboard pattern (parity-based)
    colors: blue(1) and black(0) only
  marker:
    single teal(8) pixel on a non-corner edge cell
    replaces a cell of the moving-color parity class
    exactly one of four edges (top/bottom/left/right); all four represented across examples
  moving_color: blue(1), the checkerboard parity class matching marker; compacts toward marker's edge
  bg_color: black(0), the opposite parity class
  transform:
    every row (if marker on left/right) or column (if marker on top/bottom) compacts its moving-color pixels toward the marker edge
    marker stays fixed at its edge cell
    on the marker's row/col only, cells swept by shifted moving pixels but not occupied by final compacted block become maroon(9) trail
  trail_length: 1-3 cells, proportional to grid dimension along compaction axis minus compacted count

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (checkerboard is fully determined, no search needed)
  steps:
    1. Pick H, W in [3..8]; pick an edge (top/bottom/left/right)
    2. Pick marker position on that edge, excluding corners
    3. Use moving color blue(1) and background color black(0)
    4. Fill grid with perfect checkerboard: cell (r,c) = 1 if (r+c)%2 == marker_parity, else 0
    5. Set marker cell to teal(8)
  validation: marker must not be on a corner; grid must have >=3 in each dimension so trail is non-empty
```
</generation_spec>
